    "result": "Excellent! All tests are now passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n1. **finetune/index.js** - Added named export for `APPROVAL_STATUSES` (and other schema constants). The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available through the default export. Added explicit named exports so the test can import them directly.\n\n2. **eval/metrics.js** - Fixed the `toxicityMetric` function signature. It was declared as `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms)` but the `runEvaluations` function calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`. I updated the signature to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms)` so it matches the expected calling pattern. The `references` parameter is now accepted but unused (as appropriate for a metric that only analyzes outputs), and `bannedTerms` remains an optional parameter with default values.\n\nAll 28 tests across 8 test files are now passing. \u2705",
